{"units": [{"id": "aleuo-word12", "translation": "Aleuada, patronymically from Aleuas; or one who must be guarded against. Some read it thus: aleu o da [avoid, O earth]; aleu [avoid], anachorei [withdraw], ekkline [turn aside]; and o da [O earth] means o ge [O earth]. For the Dorians call ge [earth] de and dan, and gnophon [darkness] dnophon."}, {"id": "aleuo-word13", "translation": "the"}, {"id": "aleuo-word14", "translation": "leuada"}, {"id": "aleuo-word15", "translation": "de"}, {"id": "aleuo-word16", "translation": "earth"}, {"id": "aleuo-word17", "translation": "del"}, {"id": "aleuo-word18", "translation": "Aleuada"}, {"id": "aleuo-word19", "translation": "aleu da [avoid, O earth]"}, {"id": "aleuo-word20", "translation": "aleuda"}, {"id": "aleuo-word21", "translation": "pheuda"}, {"id": "aleuo-word22", "translation": "pheu da [flee, O earth]"}, {"id": "aleuo-word23", "translation": "aleuda"}, {"id": "aleuo-word24", "translation": "of the corrector"}, {"id": "aleuo-word25", "translation": "ALEUDA"}, {"id": "aleuo-word26", "translation": "O"}, {"id": "aleuo-word27", "translation": "O"}, {"id": "aleuo-word28", "translation": "aleu da [avoid, O earth]"}, {"id": "aleuo-word29", "translation": "pau paue [stop, stop]"}, {"id": "aleuo-word30", "translation": "diain diaine [moisten, moisten]"}, {"id": "aleuo-word31", "translation": "diaine diaine [moisten, moisten]"}, {"id": "aleuo-word32", "translation": "diain diaine [moisten, moisten]"}, {"id": "aleuo-word33", "translation": "pou paue [where? stop]"}, {"id": "aleuo-word34", "translation": "diain [moisten]"}, {"id": "aleuo-word35", "translation": "pau [stop]"}, {"id": "aleuo-word36", "translation": "aleu da [avoid, O earth]"}, {"id": "aleuo-word37", "translation": "aleu [avoid]"}, {"id": "ale-orth1", "translation": "wandering"}, {"id": "ale-note1", "translation": "which drove men into wanderings."}, {"id": "ale-quote1", "translation": "And breaths coming from the Strymon, idle, hungry, hostile to men, wanderings,"}, {"id": "aletheia-orth1", "translation": "truth"}, {"id": "aletheia-def1", "translation": "truth."}, {"id": "aletheia-quote1", "translation": "Such is the boast, full of truth."}, {"id": "aletheia-quote2", "translation": "with truth (where I have restored the Doric form aletheia) he will toil in his mind."}, {"id": "aletheia-quote3", "translation": "You have entered upon this oracle with truth."}, {"id": "aletheia-quote4", "translation": "in truth."}, {"id": "aletheia-quote5", "translation": "For the words of truth are simple."}, {"id": "aletheuo-orth1", "translation": "to speak the truth"}, {"id": "aletheuo-def1", "translation": "I speak the truth."}, {"id": "aletheuo-quote1", "translation": "If the gods are willing, I would speak the truth."}, {"id": "alethes-orth1", "translation": "true"}, {"id": "alethes-def1", "translation": "true"}, {"id": "alethes-note1", "translation": "(Doric alatheis [true])"}, {"id": "alethes-note2", "translation": "where M has alethe [true], but with an alpha written above."}, {"id": "alethes-quote1", "translation": "The tongue becomes a true accuser."}, {"id": "alethes-quote2", "translation": "And the visions of dream phantoms are too true."}, {"id": "alethes-quote3", "translation": "And the revered Erinys of father Oedipus fulfilled very true things."}, {"id": "alethes-quote4", "translation": "Ares, making the father's curse true,"}, {"id": "alethes-quote5", "translation": "These things are true."}, {"id": "alethes-quote6", "translation": "whether true (changes of fire)."}, {"id": "alethes-quote7", "translation": "How then could you, speaking good things, hit upon the truth?"}, {"id": "alethes-quote8", "translation": "Know that you hear the truth."}, {"id": "alethes-quote9", "translation": "How shall I think these things true and seeing?"}, {"id": "alethes-quote10", "translation": "And I will attach all these true things to my account."}, {"id": "alethes-word1", "translation": "true (Doric)"}, {"id": "alethes-word2", "translation": "true"}, {"id": "alethes-word3", "translation": "alpha"}, {"id": "alethomantis-orth1", "translation": "true prophet"}, {"id": "alethomantis-def1", "translation": "true prophet."}, {"id": "alethomantis-quote1", "translation": "And you, being present quickly, will pity me as a true prophet."}, {"id": "alethos-orth1", "translation": "truly"}, {"id": "alethos-def1", "translation": "truly."}, {"id": "alethos-quote1", "translation": "hearing truly nothing (Schoemann reads ousin) that has been made up."}, {"id": "alethos-quote2", "translation": "The equal-voting justice came out truly."}, {"id": "alethos-quote3", "translation": "Epaphus, truly named from his deliverance."}, {"id": "alethos-quote4", "translation": "the life-giving race, which is truly of Zeus."}, {"id": "aleteia_see-orth1", "translation": "wandering"}, {"id": "aleteia_see-word1", "translation": "wandering"}, {"id": "aletes-orth1", "translation": "wanderer"}, {"id": "aletes-def1", "translation": "I wander."}, {"id": "aletes-quote1", "translation": "An exile and wanderer, a stranger to this land."}, {"id": "aletes-quote2", "translation": "But I am a wanderer, a stranger to this land."}, {"id": "alibaphes-orth1", "translation": "sea-dyed, i.e. drowned"}, {"id": "alibaphes-def1", "translation": "sea-dyed, i.e. drowned."}, {"id": "alibaphes-note1", "translation": "Thus Hermann emended what is in M: halidona (with this accent) somata polybaphe [sea-given bodies deeply dyed]."}, {"id": "alibaphes-quote1", "translation": "bodies deeply dyed by the sea."}, {"id": "alibaphes-word1", "translation": "sea-given"}, {"id": "alibaphes-word2", "translation": "bodies deeply dyed"}, {"id": "alinkios-orth1", "translation": "like"}, {"id": "alinkios-def1", "translation": "like."}, {"id": "alinkios-quote1", "translation": "like to dream shapes."}, {"id": "alidonos_see-orth1", "translation": "sea-given"}, {"id": "alidonos_see-note1", "translation": "[See halibaphes.]"}, {"id": "alidonos_see-word1", "translation": "sea-dyed"}, {"id": "alimenos-orth1", "translation": "harborless"}, {"id": "alimenos-def1", "translation": "harborless."}, {"id": "alimenos-quote1", "translation": "a harborless land."}, {"id": "alios_see-orth1", "translation": "sun"}, {"id": "alios_see-note1", "translation": "Doric for helios [sun], which see."}, {"id": "alios_see-word1", "translation": "sun"}, {"id": "alios-orth1", "translation": "of the sea"}, {"id": "alios-def1", "translation": "of the sea."}, {"id": "alios-quote1", "translation": "the sea headland common to both lands."}, {"id": "alios-quote2", "translation": "along the sea headland."}, {"id": "alios-quote3", "translation": "a sea wave."}, {"id": "alirrothos-orth1", "translation": "sea-roaring"}, {"id": "alirrothos-note1", "translation": "of the roaring sea."}, {"id": "alirrothos-quote1", "translation": "the sea-roaring straits of the ship"}, {"id": "alirrytos-orth1", "translation": "sea-flowing"}, {"id": "alirrytos-note1", "translation": "sea."}, {"id": "alirrytos-quote1", "translation": "the sea-flowing grove (thus Turnebus for alliryton)"}, {"id": "alis-orth1", "translation": "enough"}, {"id": "alis-def1", "translation": "enough."}, {"id": "alis-quote1", "translation": "But it is enough for Argive men to come to blows with Cadmeans."}, {"id": "alis-quote2", "translation": "You were enough of an enemy by the Scamander."}, {"id": "alis-quote3", "translation": "And there is enough of suffering."}, {"id": "alis-quote4", "translation": "But if there should be enough of these toils, we would accept it."}, {"id": "alis-quote5", "translation": "as enough has been said."}, {"id": "aliskomai-orth1", "translation": "to be captured"}, {"id": "aliskomai-def1", "translation": "I am captured."}, {"id": "aliskomai-note1", "translation": "(with perfect healoka, aorist healon, whose subjunctive is halo, participle halous)"}, {"id": "aliskomai-quote1", "translation": "the city having been captured,"}, {"id": "aliskomai-quote2", "translation": "the gods who protect the city, those of the captured land."}, {"id": "aliskomai-quote3", "translation": "just as men whose city is captured."}, {"id": "aliskomai-quote4", "translation": "and the fatherland captured by the spear through your zeal"}, {"id": "aliskomai-quote5", "translation": "if indeed the city of Ilium has been captured."}, {"id": "aliskomai-quote6", "translation": "both of the captured and of the victors."}, {"id": "aliskomai-quote7", "translation": "captured by others."}, {"id": "aliskomai-quote8", "translation": "and the city, captured by smoke, is still conspicuous."}, {"id": "aliskomai-quote9", "translation": "And now you see these mad women captured."}]}